MCQ Question Paper

Q1. In the KompoZer 'Table Properties' dialog, what is the distinct difference between 'Spacing' and 'Padding'?
A. Spacing is between cells; Padding is between the cell border and content.
B. Spacing is internal to the cell; Padding is external.
C. Spacing controls border width; Padding controls cell height.
D. There is no difference; they are synonyms.

Q2. Which method places the cursor inside a specific form element?
A. select()
B. click()
C. focus()
D. place()

Q3. When creating a table in KompoZer, the 'Width' can be defined in which two units?
A. Inches and Pixels
B. Pixels and % of window
C. Points and Centimeters
D. Em and Px

Q4. Which String constructor creates a string from a character array?
A. String(char ary[])
B. String(char c)
C. String(int[] ary)
D. String(byte b)

Q5. Which of the following is a valid hexadecimal literal in Java?
A. 0x1G
B. 0xFF7A
C. #FF7A
D. hFF7A

Q6. Which statement is used to display output to the screen?
A. System.in.read()
B. System.out.println()
C. print()
D. echo()

Q7. What does the `rows` attribute of a `<textarea>` tag specify?
A. The width of the text area
B. The number of visible lines of text
C. The character limit
D. The font weight

Q8. Which statement allows you to skip the current iteration of a loop?
A. break
B. skip
C. continue
D. return

Q9. Which tab in the CSS dialog allows you to set an image as the background?
A. Box
B. Text
C. Background
D. Lists

Q10. In the 'Advanced Property Editor' for adding JavaScript, why is the keyword `return` used in `return validateForm()`?
A. To call the function twice.
B. To ensure the form does NOT submit if the function returns false.
C. To refresh the page.
D. To return the focus to the window.

Q11. What does the expression `new Room()` return?
